Runtime dependencies
--------------------
The Debian installer includes the exact Python wheels in requirements.lock.
These are separate upstream works, not relicensed as DictaDesk code. Their
copyright and license files are retained under /usr/lib/dictadesk/vendor,
including each distribution's .dist-info directory and bundled library notices.

Acknowledgments include ONNX Runtime, onnx-asr, Moonshine Voice, NumPy,
FlatBuffers, Hugging Face Hub, sounddevice/PortAudio, python-xlib, keyring,
SecretStorage, cryptography and their dependencies. Source project URLs and
versions are retained in the installed wheel metadata. FlatBuffers' Python
wheel omits the full Apache 2.0 text; packaging/licenses/Apache-2.0.txt supplies
it alongside the preserved Copyright 2014 Google Inc. notices in its source.
System libraries such as Python, GTK, libadwaita, GLib, PyGObject and PortAudio
are installed by the distribution package manager and retain their own licenses.

Models are downloaded separately, never bundled in the repository or installer:
- Parakeet: https://huggingface.co/nvidia/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v3
- ONNX exports: https://huggingface.co/istupakov
- Moonshine Tiny English: https://huggingface.co/moonshine-ai/moonshine-tiny
- Whisper: https://github.com/openai/whisper
- Whisper Tiny ONNX: https://huggingface.co/onnx-community/whisper-tiny
Model cards and repositories describe each model's licensing and limitations.

Evaluation references and public-sample attribution are in tests/MODEL-EVALUATION.rst.
No downloaded model or evaluation audio is included in source control.
